From: Joel Wiramu Pauling <aenertia@aenertia.net>
Date: Sun, 2 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +1300
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: dw_mmc: add PRV_DAT_WAIT to CMD52 for SDIO device
 compatibility

The Designware MMC controller can issue CMD52 (SD_IO_RW_DIRECT)
without waiting for a previous data transfer to complete, since CMD52
has no data phase and the current code only sets SDMMC_CMD_PRV_DAT_WAIT
when cmd->data is non-NULL.

On certain SDIO devices (notably the Seekwave SV6160/RK915 WiFi chip),
this causes bus collisions: a CMD52 register read interleaved with an
in-flight CMD53 data transfer corrupts the DW MMC controller state,
leading to data CRC errors (RINTSTS bit 16) and subsequent CMD53 read
timeouts (-110 ETIMEDOUT).

Add SDMMC_CMD_PRV_DAT_WAIT to all SD_IO_RW_DIRECT commands, not just
CCCR_ABORT.  This makes the controller wait for any previous data
transfer to complete before issuing CMD52, preventing bus collisions.

This is safe for all SDIO devices -- waiting for data completion before
a register access is correct protocol behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Joel Wiramu Pauling <aenertia@aenertia.net>
---
 drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
@@ -263,7 +263,14 @@
 	    (cmd->opcode == SD_IO_RW_DIRECT &&
 	     ((cmd->arg >> 9) & 0x1FFFF) == SDIO_CCCR_ABORT))
 		cmdr |= SDMMC_CMD_STOP;
-	else if (cmd->opcode != MMC_SEND_STATUS && cmd->data)
+	else if (cmd->opcode == SD_IO_RW_DIRECT)
+		/*
+		 * CMD52 has no data phase but must still wait for any
+		 * previous CMD53 data transfer to complete.  Without
+		 * this, CMD52 can collide with in-flight data on the
+		 * bus, corrupting controller state.
+		 */
+		cmdr |= SDMMC_CMD_PRV_DAT_WAIT;
+	else if (cmd->opcode != MMC_SEND_STATUS && cmd->data)
 		cmdr |= SDMMC_CMD_PRV_DAT_WAIT;

 	if (cmd->opcode == SD_SWITCH_VOLTAGE) {
